<article class="env-definition" id="08IP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08IP">Definition <span data-tag="08IP">75.20.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $X$, $Y$ be algebraic spaces over $B$. We say $X$ and $Y$ are <em>Tor independent over $B$</em> if and only if for every commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \ar[d]_{\overline{y}} \ar[dr]_{\overline{b}} \ar[r]_-{\overline{x}} &  X \ar[d] \\  Y \ar[r] &  B }  \]
</div>
  <p> of geometric points the rings $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ and $\mathcal{O}_{Y, \overline{y}}$ are Tor independent over $\mathcal{O}_{B, \overline{b}}$ (see More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/0660" data-tag="0660">15.62.1</a>). </p>
</article>